## Break
`break` exits a loop immediately:

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)
{
    if (i == 5) break;
    Console.WriteLine(i);
}
// 0, 1, 2, 3, 4
```

## Continue
`continue` skips the rest of the current iteration:

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++)
{
    if (i == 3) continue;
    Console.WriteLine(i);
}
// 0, 1, 2, 4, 5
```


